# RulesApp Study Mode pilot — content-hashed runtime assets.
#
# Each filename encodes a hash of that file's content, so the bytes must be
# identical on every checkout. Git's CRLF normalisation would rewrite them
# per-platform while leaving the hashed name unchanged — a file that claims,
# by its own name, to be something it no longer is. Never normalise these.
* -text
